                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As a game Adventurezator leaves a lot to be desired. The story and the puzzles are simplistic, the 'action' is aggravating. Being eaten by a bear in suspenders is less fun than it sounds. Especially if it happens over and over, thanks to clumsy controls. Even picking stuff up or going through doors is unnecessarily complicated.  I didn't get very far into the story before getting thoroughly frustrated. \nThe lack of content on the workshop three months after release, might be a sign, that Adventurezator isn't a good game engine, either. For me the biggest issue is the inability to import my own assets. The models in the game are just too limited. The lack of any kind of scripting means, that I could only make the same style of unappealing action/adventure game as the builtin campaign.\nThe best part of Adventurezator is the cutscene editor. It's really easy to use. Pigasus Games should turn it into a standalone tool with export to video an GIF. I'd buy that.",
